{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1613 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "18cd1d23b7cc408c4d4b4db379184330a33d9499259bf0ac055306a94cf4f558" :edb/db-before-t 1612 :edb/db-after-t 1613 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534925 50 #inst "2026-10-08T11:10:39.284Z" 13194139534925 true] [17592186171888 1020 #edb/ref 17592186320328 13194139534925 true] [17592186171889 1020 #edb/ref 17592186320335 13194139534925 true] [17592186172523 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534925 true] [17592186172523 1100 "Determine the value of $(\\frac{4}{2})$." 13194139534925 false] [17592186172523 1100 "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}).$" 13194139534925 true] [17592186172523 1145 "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=4$ and $r=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}) & =\\frac{4!}{(4-2)!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2!}{2!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3\\cdot \\cancel{2!}}{2\\cdot \\cancel{2!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534925 true] [17592186172524 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534925 true] [17592186172524 1100 "Determine the value of $(\\frac{6}{3})$." 13194139534925 false] [17592186172524 1100 "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3}).$" 13194139534925 true] [17592186172524 1145 "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=6$ and $r=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3}) & =\\frac{6!}{(6-3)!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3!}{3!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{6}\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot \\cancel{3!}}{\\cancel{3\\cdot 2}\\cdot \\cancel{3!}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320328 1017 #edb/ref 17592186320329 13194139534925 true] [17592186320328 1089 "q-69726" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320328 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534925 true] [17592186320328 1100 "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3})=[]+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{3})\n$$" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320328 1113 #uuid "efb5ff53-fd96-5b59-9204-3a3f9833789e" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320328 1145 "To find $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $5$ and position $3$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{3}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{4}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{5}) \\\\  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3})=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2})+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{3})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}).$" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320330 13194139534925 true] [17592186320329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320331 13194139534925 true] [17592186320329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320332 13194139534925 true] [17592186320329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320333 13194139534925 true] [17592186320329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320334 13194139534925 true] [17592186320329 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534925 true] [17592186320329 1041 "selection" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320329 1104 #edb/ref 17592186320333 13194139534925 true] [17592186320329 1110 #uuid "265cbbe6-898d-5330-ab5b-06a03de83229" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320330 1034 "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1})" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320330 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534925 true] [17592186320330 1111 #uuid "d36fbb04-29f5-5084-b628-7d720327696b" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320331 1034 "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2})" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320331 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534925 true] [17592186320331 1111 #uuid "ef9fa87e-82e5-5776-b8be-e9cefb135eed" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320332 1034 "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{0})" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320332 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534925 true] [17592186320332 1111 #uuid "8b85e2cf-d91f-5a6d-8f0e-f4da229ede82" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320333 1034 "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2})" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320333 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534925 true] [17592186320333 1111 #uuid "3191bdf0-1e28-5130-bc4a-afd31186518c" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320334 1034 "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{3})" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320334 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534925 true] [17592186320334 1111 #uuid "1ed03ce9-97ce-5fbe-be72-4fd735cf805c" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320335 1017 #edb/ref 17592186320336 13194139534925 true] [17592186320335 1089 "q-70306" 13194139534925 true] [17592186320335 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534925 tru